    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0572",
      "reading_order": 604,
      "section": "Flushing and Cleaning",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 706.5248068359375,
        "r": 291.60370000000023,
        "b": 646.0400492035388
      },
      "content": "Once a year, drain, flush and refill the cooling system with new coolant.  To drain the system, open the radiator coolant drain and the cylinder block drain on the the rear (non-service access) side of engine. See Figure 8-2.",
      "hyperlink_hint": true,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_603",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_603",
          "title": "Flushing and Cleaning"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0573",
      "reading_order": 605,
      "section": "Flushing and Cleaning",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.565599999999996,
        "t": 630.3862068359375,
        "r": 291.44990000000007,
        "b": 595.1839519502827
      },
      "content": "WARNING Contact with hot coolant can cause severe burns.  Do not bleed hot, pressurized coolant from a closed cooling system.",
      "severity": "warning",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_603",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_603",
          "title": "Flushing and Cleaning"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "admonition",
      "semantic_role": "warning",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0574",
      "reading_order": 606,
      "section": "Flushing and Cleaning",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.565599999999996,
        "t": 571.7661068359375,
        "r": 291.9229,
        "b": 511.2241492035388
      },
      "content": "Chemical Cleaning: Rust and scale slow heat absorption and can block coolant flow.  Clean the cooling system if rust and scale have collected on the engine water jacket or in the heat exchanger.   Use a good cleaning compound and follow its instructions.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_603",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_603",
          "title": "Flushing and Cleaning"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0575",
      "reading_order": 607,
      "section": "Flushing and Cleaning",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.56560000000002,
        "t": 487.8042068359375,
        "r": 291.4730000000002,
        "b": 427.31944920353885
      },
      "content": "Flushing: After cleaning, or before filling the system with new coolant, drain the system and fill with clean water.  Run the generator set for 10 minutes, then drain the system completely.  Refill with the coolant mixture.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_603",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_603",
          "title": "Flushing and Cleaning"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0576",
      "reading_order": 608,
      "section": "Flushing and Cleaning",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5645,
        "t": 402.7641068359375,
        "r": 291.8018999999996,
        "b": 342.27725195028273
      },
      "content": "CAUTION Never pour hot water into a cold engine or cold water into a hot engine.  Doing so can crack the head or the cylinder block.  Do not operate the unit without water for even a few minutes.",
      "severity": "caution",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_603",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
