      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0579",
      "reading_order": 611,
      "section": "Pressure Cap",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 197.8002068359375,
        "r": 125.03860000000003,
        "b": 186.98094696067756
      },
      "content": "Pressure Cap",
      "level": 2,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_611",
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_611",
          "title": "Pressure Cap"
        }
      ],
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "section_heading",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0580",
      "reading_order": 612,
      "section": "Pressure Cap",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 166.2979068359375,
        "r": 291.38590000000033,
        "b": 105.81314920353873
      },
      "content": "Closed cooling systems use a pressure cap to increase the boiling point of the coolant and allow higher operating temperatures.  Replace the pressure cap every two years, or sooner if it malfunctions.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_611",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_611",
          "title": "Pressure Cap"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0581",
      "reading_order": 613,
      "section": "FAN BELT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 413.915,
        "t": 738.0270068359374,
        "r": 471.76219999999984,
        "b": 727.2077469606776
      },
      "content": "FAN BELT",
      "level": 2,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_613",
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_613",
          "title": "FAN BELT"
        }
      ],
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "section_heading",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0582",
      "reading_order": 614,
      "section": "FAN BELT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 718.5436068359375,
        "r": 564.7799999999996,
        "b": 683.3434492035387
      },
      "content": "A loose fan belt can cause the engine to overheat. The belt tension must be correct for the set to run well.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_613",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_613",
          "title": "FAN BELT"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0583",
      "reading_order": 615,
      "section": "FAN BELT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 670.5253068359375,
        "r": 564.7612999999997,
        "b": 647.9674492035388
      },
      "content": "First,  remove  the  generator  set's  starting  battery cables (negative [-] cable first).",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_613",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_613",
          "title": "FAN BELT"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0584",
      "reading_order": 616,
      "section": "FAN BELT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9388,
        "t": 638.3232068359375,
        "r": 564.9375000000006,
        "b": 565.1940519502828
      },
      "content": "WARNING Accidental  starting  of  the  set  can cause severe personal injury or death.  Stop the generator set and disable it by disconnecting the  starting  battery  cables  (negative  [-]  cable first) when maintaining or repairing the engine, controls, or generator.",
      "severity": "warning",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_613",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_613",
          "title": "FAN BELT"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "admonition",
      "semantic_role": "warning",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0585",
      "reading_order": 617,
      "section": "FAN BELT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9388,
        "t": 552.3780068359376,
        "r": 564.9803999999982,
        "b": 517.1757519502828
      },
      "content": "To reach the fan belt, remove the belt guard from the front of the set. Do not operate the generator set without the belt guard in place.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_613",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_613",
          "title": "FAN BELT"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0586",
      "reading_order": 618,
      "section": "FAN BELT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9388,
        "t": 504.3597068359377,
        "r": 564.7614999999997,
        "b": 456.517249203539
      },
      "content": "To  adjust  the  belt,  loosen  the  bolt  that  passes through  the  long  slot  in  the  alternator  mounting bracket and slide the alternator until the tension is right.  See Figure 8-3.",
      "hyperlink_hint": true,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_613",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_613",
          "title": "FAN BELT"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0587",
      "reading_order": 619,
      "section": "FAN BELT",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9388,
        "t": 443.69910683593776,
        "r": 564.8594,
        "b": 408.49894920353904
      },
      "content": "Belt tension is correct when a finger pressure of 22 pounds (10 kg) at the middle of the belt deflects it about 0.4 inch (10 mm).",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_613",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_8",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_8",
          "title": "8. Routine Maintenance"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_613",
          "title": "FAN BELT"
        }
      ],
      "page": 50,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
